            "activitySource": 1,
            "sourceData": {
              "fabricAnswer": "I’m not able to get a valid result from the available data tools for this question. The tooling interface is rejecting the queries needed to analyze sales patterns from the lakehouse (it reports the query as “irrelevant to the data schema”), so I can’t reliably compute or describe actual “latest sales trends” from your dataset.\n\nBecause of the anti-hallucination rules I’m following, I’m not allowed to guess or invent trend data. To move forward, I’d need either:\n\n- A different or more specific question that doesn’t require computing trends from the tools (for example, about the structure of your products/categories/stores), or  \n- Direct access to a table that actually contains sales or orders (with measures like quantity sold, revenue, timestamps) so I can query it via the tool.\n\nIf you can share what sales/transactions table you have (or confirm that such a table exists in your environment), I can rephrase the query accordingly and try again. Otherwise, I can outline how you would calculate “latest sales trends” conceptually (KPIs to track, queries to run, and how to interpret them), but that would be generic guidance rather than results from your actual data.",
